1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,376
Running a luxury hotel group means running many businesses at once.

2
00:00:05,426 --> 00:00:10,763
Hotels, restaurants, waterparks, shops and spas, across several countries.

3
00:00:12,113 --> 00:00:16,074
Each one has its own systems, and its own version of the numbers.

4
00:00:16,124 --> 00:00:22,059
So even simple questions, like how full are we, and are we making money, can take days to answer.

5
00:00:23,309 --> 00:00:26,023
This is the Hospitality Intelligence Platform.

6
00:00:26,073 --> 00:00:29,087
A working prototype that brings all of it together.

7
00:00:30,087 --> 00:00:33,143
Every part of the business is here, in a single menu.

8
00:00:33,193 --> 00:00:36,190
Let's look at the problems it solves, one at a time.

9
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:39,661
The first problem is scattered data.

10
00:00:39,711 --> 00:00:46,535
Different hotels use different booking systems, and every property calculates occupancy and profit in its own way.

11
00:00:47,785 --> 00:00:51,867
The platform collects thirty six feeds from every source system.

12
00:00:51,917 --> 00:00:55,548
Then it cleans, matches and checks them, in three stages.

13
00:00:56,798 --> 00:00:58,839
The result is one trusted view.

14
00:00:58,889 --> 00:01:04,504
This is the executive dashboard, covering every property and every line of business.

15
00:01:05,504 --> 00:01:12,536
Revenue, occupancy, room rate and profit are each defined once, and shown the same way to everyone.

16
00:01:13,536 --> 00:01:18,420
Any leader can compare properties side by side, then open the one that needs attention.

17
00:01:19,770 --> 00:01:20,958
The second problem.

18
00:01:21,008 --> 00:01:22,783
Reports only look backwards.

19
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:27,800
By the time they arrive, the month is over, and next month is anyone's guess.

20
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:33,174
Here, every part of the business is forecast up to ninety days ahead.

21
00:01:33,224 --> 00:01:35,048
The blue line is what happened.

22
00:01:35,098 --> 00:01:39,403
The orange line is what the model expects, with its range of confidence.

23
00:01:40,403 --> 00:01:43,449
Each forecast is tested against real outcomes.

24
00:01:43,499 --> 00:01:46,612
For this hotel, the error is about ten percent.

25
00:01:46,662 --> 00:01:48,631
Better than a simple baseline.

26
00:01:49,981 --> 00:01:51,717
Third, revenue slips away.

27
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:53,846
Rooms sit empty in quiet weeks.

28
00:01:53,896 --> 00:01:56,250
Rates stay low when demand is high.

29
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:58,929
And bookings cancel too late to resell.

30
00:02:00,179 --> 00:02:03,440
The hotel dashboard shows the next sixty days.

31
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:08,047
Bookings already made, in blue, against the forecast, in orange.

32
00:02:09,047 --> 00:02:12,731
Where a week looks soft, the platform recommends a promotion.

33
00:02:12,781 --> 00:02:15,914
Where demand is strong, it recommends raising rates.

34
00:02:15,964 --> 00:02:19,097
And it flags the reservations most likely to cancel.

35
00:02:20,447 --> 00:02:23,033
Fourth, each department works in the dark.

36
00:02:24,283 --> 00:02:26,309
So every team gets its own view.

37
00:02:26,359 --> 00:02:30,073
Park managers see queue times, by attraction, and by hour.

38
00:02:31,323 --> 00:02:35,150
Chefs see every dish ranked by profit, and which ones to reprice.

39
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:42,747
And retail managers see which products will run out before the next delivery, and how much to order.

40
00:02:44,097 --> 00:02:46,183
Fifth, costs creep up quietly.

41
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:47,678
A utility bill jumps.

42
00:02:47,728 --> 00:02:49,458
A supplier raises prices.

43
00:02:49,508 --> 00:02:52,163
Discounts appear that nobody approved.

44
00:02:53,413 --> 00:02:57,313
The platform watches for anything unusual, and raises an alert.

45
00:02:57,363 --> 00:03:00,322
To test it, we hid several problems in the data.

46
00:03:00,372 --> 00:03:01,513
It found every one.

47
00:03:02,513 --> 00:03:06,573
Each alert is assigned to an owner, and tracked until it is resolved.

48
00:03:07,923 --> 00:03:12,656
Sixth, buildings waste energy, and equipment fails without warning.

49
00:03:13,906 --> 00:03:19,744
The energy page compares what each property used, with what its occupancy and weather justify.

50
00:03:19,794 --> 00:03:21,937
The gap between the lines is waste.

51
00:03:22,937 --> 00:03:25,551
It brings the important findings to the top.

52
00:03:25,601 --> 00:03:26,883
A probable water leak.

53
00:03:26,933 --> 00:03:27,973
An energy anomaly.

54
00:03:28,023 --> 00:03:30,213
And service contracts about to lapse.

55
00:03:31,213 --> 00:03:38,518
It also scores more than six thousand devices, from door locks to chillers, for their chance of failing in the next thirty days.

56
00:03:38,568 --> 00:03:40,242
So they can be serviced first.

57
00:03:41,592 --> 00:03:42,400
And finally.

58
00:03:42,450 --> 00:03:47,696
Insight is useless without action, and people are right to be wary of AI

59
00:03:47,746 --> 00:03:48,984
acting on its own.

60
00:03:50,234 --> 00:03:56,859
So every recommendation is listed with its priority, its estimated value, and the model's confidence.

61
00:03:58,109 --> 00:04:00,753
Open one, and you see the evidence behind it.

62
00:04:02,003 --> 00:04:03,786
Nothing happens automatically.

63
00:04:03,836 --> 00:04:08,431
An authorised person approves or rejects it, and every decision is recorded.

64
00:04:09,781 --> 00:04:10,753
One trusted view.

65
00:04:10,803 --> 00:04:13,218
Forecasts for every part of the business.

66
00:04:13,268 --> 00:04:15,742
And clear actions, with people in control.

67
00:04:15,792 --> 00:04:19,889
What you have seen is a working prototype, running on synthetic data.

68
00:04:19,939 --> 00:04:22,594
The next step is to connect the real systems.

69
00:04:22,644 --> 00:04:23,977
Thank you for watching.
